            <ArticleTitle>[Antipyretic and anti-inflammatory effects of Artemisia annua L].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>44-8, 63-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The antipyretic, heat-resisting anti-inflammatory analgesic and bacteriostasis effects of water extracts ethyl-acetate and n-butyl alcohol extracts of Artemisia annua are reported. Animal experiment has demonstrated that qinghao acid is one of the actively bacteriostatic constituents. Scopoletin is one of the anti-inflammatory constituents of Artemisia annua.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
